From 13379314fdb2d5ad7ba8484f938a95b5ea383aac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:57:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 58/60] u/comp/wmr: CPU-affinity experiment knobs + controller
 keepalive v2 (client-independent)

Two round-2 deliverables (T204 program). (1) XRT_COMPOSITOR_CPU_AFFINITY /
WMR_CPU_AFFINITY: env-gated CPU pinning for the compositor's three RT threads and
the WMR read + constellation processing threads -- strict no-op unset. Investigation
first confirmed RT priority is already comprehensively applied (no missing-RT
hypothesis survives); the live suspects for the 4-7% one-slot-late frames are the
kernel's RT bandwidth throttle (sched_rt_runtime_us=950000 reserves 5% for non-RT,
numerically matching the 4-4.4% floor -- root A/B pending) and cache/SMT contention,
which the affinity knobs let us test. (2) Keepalive v2: the periodic controller
resend now ticks from wmr_run_thread once per loop -- client-independent, fixing
0054's self-invalidating query-driven design (0 resends with 0 clients, T203/T204).
The receive-path alternative was rejected for a real self-deadlock: the tunnel
callback holds conn->lock which send_bytes re-takes. get_tracked_pose call removed
(run-thread tick strictly dominates).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
